## Location
rust/lichen-rpl/src/dodag.rs:397-403

## Issue
When `parents.len() >= MAX_PARENT_CANDIDATES` and a new (not existing) neighbor sends a valid DIO, the candidate is silently discarded but `DioOutcome::Accepted` is returned.

```rust
} else if self.parents.len() < MAX_PARENT_CANDIDATES {
    // Insert new parent only if under limit
    self.parents.insert(neighbor_addr, candidate);
}
// else: at capacity with a new parent -> reject silently
self.select_parent();
DioOutcome::Accepted  // <-- misleading
```

## Trigger
- Node has 16 parent candidates tracked
- A 17th neighbor sends a valid DIO
- Caller sees `Accepted` but parent is not tracked

## Impact
Callers cannot distinguish "accepted and tracked" from "accepted but discarded". A trickle timer or diagnostic code expecting the neighbor to be a known parent will find it missing with no indication of why.

## Suggested fix
Return a new variant `DioOutcome::AtCapacity` or at minimum `DioOutcome::Rejected` when the parent table is full and the candidate is not already tracked.
